##### FUTURES code for EBCI Long View Project; Using data from 2000-2014 for calibration, 2015-2024 for validation, and 2025-2100 for future projections.
##### Note: Redoing previous simulations in new location (secas_sbre_aligned) set to NAD83 / Conus Albers (EPSG:5070) so that everything is in the same projection and uses the same computational region to avoid misalignement issues
##### Keep all input data in PERMANENT, and use separate mapsets for SSP1, SSP2, and SSP5 simulations

######################################################################## INITIAL STEPS AND DATA PREPARATION ########################################################################

### Created the location secas_sbre_aligned and selected EPSG: 5070 as the projection (datum transformation option 1)

### Used PERMANENT as the mapset where the inputs will be, and created new mapsets to store SSP1, SSP2, and SSP5 scenario results

# make sure we are in the PERMANENT mapset
g.mapset mapset=PERMANENT

# import the SECAS Blueprint dataset to ensure it is 30m and use as the alignment reference
r.in.gdal input=D:\conservation_datasets\SEBlueprint20251204\5_Priorities\Blueprint2025.tif output=Blueprint2025

# inspect
r.info -g map=Blueprint2025

# import counties shapefile to determine study area 
v.import input=D:\FUTURES\Data\counties\counties_final.shp output=counties

# inspect
v.info -g map=counties_final

# most recent landuse layer to help set computational region and grid alignment
r.import input=D:\nlcd_annual_data\Annual_NLCD_LndCov_2024_CU_C1V1\Annual_NLCD_LndCov_2024_CU_C1V1.tif output=landuse_2024 resample=nearest (align? res=30m?)

# set the computational region to the county boundaries vector, but align it with the landuse raster
g.region vector=counties align=landuse_2024 -p

#
g.region save=study_area_30m



